pack install pipeline
├── when staging a valid pack from a path
│   ├── it copies only the manifest closure
│   ├── it names the staging dir after the manifest name
│   └── it validates the staged copy with the loader
├── when the source contains a symlink
│   └── it refuses the install
├── when a source file exceeds the size cap
│   └── it refuses the install
├── when the manifest name is not a single path component
│   └── it refuses the install
├── when committing a staged pack
│   ├── it installs under the manifest name
│   ├── it writes a receipt with file digests
│   └── it removes the staging directory
├── when the name is already installed
│   ├── it refuses without force
│   └── it swaps atomically with force
├── when a staged install is dropped without commit
│   └── it leaves no staging residue
├── when verifying against a curated index entry
│   ├── it accepts matching digests
│   └── it rejects a tampered file
├── when installing from a git source
│   └── it clones resolves and stages the pack
├── when removing an installed pack
│   ├── it deletes the pack directory
│   ├── it refuses a name with path separators
│   ├── it refuses a symlinked entry
│   └── it refuses a missing pack
└── when generating the curated index
    ├── it skips packs whose closure is not fully tracked
    └── it matches the committed index
